messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI copilots become routine in work and education.",
      "detail": "Safety audits and model provenance standards mature across major markets. Global warming is about 1.2–1.4°C above preindustrial, and adaptation spending accelerates."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Malaria and other vaccine rollouts cut child mortality substantially.",
      "detail": "Cheap mRNA and protein-based vaccines scale in Africa and South Asia. Electric vehicles exceed 30% of new global auto sales."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Global mean temperature crosses 1.5°C on a sustained basis.",
      "detail": "Exceedances that were once rare become frequent, pushing adaptation and loss-and-damage finance higher."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Post-quantum cryptography is widely deployed on the public internet.",
      "detail": "Most critical infrastructure rotates to quantum-resistant algorithms; legacy systems persist but shrink."
    },
    {
      "year": 2034,
      "event": "Autonomous logistics mainstreams in wealthy regions.",
      "detail": "Ports, warehouses, and long-haul trucking see pervasive autonomy; labor shifts toward supervision, maintenance, and customer-facing roles."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "General-purpose AI reaches top-human performance on many professional tasks.",
      "detail": "Productivity jumps in software, research, design, and services; institutions adopt guardrails to manage errors and misuse."
    },
    {
      "year": 2036,
      "event": "A major great-power crisis de-escalates after near-miss incidents.",
      "detail": "Renewed arms-control talks, hotlines, and autonomous-weapons norms follow, reducing acute nuclear risk for a time."
    },
    {
      "year": 2037,
      "event": "A permanently crewed international lunar base begins in-situ resource operations.",
      "detail": "Regolith processing for oxygen, water, and building materials reaches pilot scale; continuous habitation becomes the norm."
    },
    {
      "year": 2039,
      "event": "First crewed Mars expedition achieves a short-stay landing and safe return.",
      "detail": "Stays are measured in weeks, leveraging pre-positioned supplies and rapid transit windows."
    },
    {
      "year": 2041,
      "event": "A global biosurveillance network achieves sub-week pathogen detection at scale.",
      "detail": "Wastewater, clinical, and environmental sequencing enable early outbreak alerts and targeted responses."
    },
    {
      "year": 2042,
      "event": "A grid-connected fusion pilot intermittently delivers net electricity.",
      "detail": "Costs remain high, but a commercial path is visible alongside fission, renewables, and storage."
    },
    {
      "year": 2044,
      "event": "Planetary defense reaches full operating capability.",
      "detail": "All near-Earth objects above ~140 m are cataloged, and a proven kinetic deflection architecture stands ready."
    },
    {
      "year": 2046,
      "event": "Ultra-efficient power electronics and next-gen batteries slash storage costs.",
      "detail": "Seasonal storage and industrial electrification expand rapidly, pushing fossil generation into steep decline."
    },
    {
      "year": 2048,
      "event": "A significant respiratory pandemic is contained within a year.",
      "detail": "Rapid vaccine design, stockpiled antivirals, and ventilation upgrades limit mortality compared to COVID-19."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global net CO2 emissions approach zero; warming nears ~2.0°C.",
      "detail": "Megacity retrofits for heat, flood, and water stress become standard practice; climate damages persist but are better managed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2052,
      "event": "Robust global AI governance compacts take hold.",
      "detail": "Safety certification, compute accountability, and limits on autonomous weapons are widely adopted, lowering systemic AI risk."
    },
    {
      "year": 2054,
      "event": "World population peaks around 9.7–10.1 billion and begins to decline.",
      "detail": "Aging societies struggle with care and pensions; migration and automation cushion workforce gaps."
    },
    {
      "year": 2058,
      "event": "Carbon removal scales to 5–10 GtCO2 per year.",
      "detail": "Forestry, soil, DAC, and mineralization all contribute; net-negative pathways begin to pull concentrations down slowly."
    },
    {
      "year": 2063,
      "event": "A limited, temporary stratospheric aerosol program caps peak extremes.",
      "detail": "Run under international oversight with defined exit ramps, it buys time for emissions cuts and removals, then tapers."
    },
    {
      "year": 2068,
      "event": "Africa becomes the largest engine of net-new global growth.",
      "detail": "Manufacturing corridors, a pan-African grid, and services exports expand rapidly as education and health outcomes improve."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Average healthy lifespan rises by 10–20 years in many countries.",
      "detail": "Gene therapies, cancer vaccines, and organ bioengineering reduce mortality from major diseases; aging remains but is better managed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2085,
      "event": "Managed retreat from the most vulnerable coasts largely completes.",
      "detail": "New inland and elevated coastal cities replace high-risk zones; insurance and finance adapt to long-run climate realities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2095,
      "event": "Noninvasive brain–computer interfaces become commonplace.",
      "detail": "They are used for communication, rehabilitation, and work augmentation; privacy and cognitive rights frameworks stabilize."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Sea level rises 0.5–1.0 m versus 2000; warming stabilizes near 2.1–2.3°C.",
      "detail": "Some low-lying nations complete partial relocations; food and energy systems prove resilient but require ongoing adaptation."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "Self-sufficient lunar and Martian settlements reach the low thousands in population.",
      "detail": "Closed-loop life support, local manufacturing, and tele-robotic industry underpin permanence beyond Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Beamed-sail interstellar probes are launched at ~0.1c.",
      "detail": "Targets include nearby Sun-like and red-dwarf systems; first data returns arrive decades later, informing exoplanet science."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "Designed ecosystems restore biodiversity corridors on multiple continents.",
      "detail": "Rewilded regions and climate-resilient species mixes stabilize many biomes, though extinctions leave lasting gaps."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Abundant clean energy supports near-post-scarcity conditions on Earth.",
      "detail": "Fusion, fission, renewables, storage, and space-based solar underpin high living standards with modest material footprints."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Humanity diversifies into biological, cybernetic, and digital clades with legal personhood.",
      "detail": "Interclade norms emerge around autonomy, reproduction, and data rights; many people remain baseline human by choice."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Sea level reaches 2–3 m above 2000; global coastlines are permanently reshaped.",
      "detail": "New ports and inland waterways redefine trade; some mega-deltas and islands are lost or transformed."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Mars hosts millions in domed cities with limited climate modification.",
      "detail": "Partial terraforming slightly warms and thickens the atmosphere but requires continuous maintenance."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Large solar-power constellations and inner–solar system mining are routine.",
      "detail": "Partial swarms of collectors increase available power orders of magnitude without enclosing the Sun."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Outer–solar system habitats achieve full autarky and cultural distinctiveness.",
      "detail": "Radiation-hardened O’Neill structures and icy-moon facilities support independent lifeways and economies."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "First small interstellar settlements exist within 50 light-years.",
      "detail": "Travel remains rare and slow; communications are asynchronous, leading to divergent cultures but shared heritage."
    },
    {
      "year": 6000,
      "event": "Deep-time knowledge institutions safeguard collective memory across sites.",
      "detail": "Redundant archives on Earth, the Moon, and in deep space preserve languages, science, and histories through upheavals."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Atmospheric CO2 approaches preindustrial levels; a new glacial cycle remains delayed.",
      "detail": "Sea level is near its multi-millennial peak and begins an extremely slow decline if net-negative emissions persist."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Human-descended civilizations span the Solar System and nearby stars.",
      "detail": "Baseline Homo sapiens may persist alongside derived clades, but continuity depends on cultural choices, governance, and gene flow over millennia."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "uncertain",
  "summary": "Humanity likely survives this century’s climate, demographic, and technological transitions, stabilizing warming near ~2°C and building a resilient, high-energy, low-emissions civilization with transformative AI. Over millennia, we diversify biologically and digitally and gradually expand into the Solar System and nearby stars, while culture, governance, and ethics determine cohesion more than technology does. By year 10000, descendants of today’s humans almost certainly exist, but whether baseline Homo sapiens is continuous and recognizable is genuinely uncertain."
}
